<title>PORTUGAL: Cimpor sags as new shares quoted.</title>
<headline>Cimpor sags as new shares quoted.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Cimpor-Cimentos de Portugal fell nearly two percent pct to 3,430 escudos as several million shares from its privatisation became available for trade.</p>
<p>But the stock was above its 3,406 escudo low. Traders said the cement stock should draw support around the 3,400 level.</p>
<p>&quot;There is good support at 3,400 escudos...I don't think it will go below that,&quot; said one trader who asked not to be named.</p>
<p>Employees, small investors and emigrants, who were allotted some 13.5 million shares at the privatisation six months ago, could trade the shares for the first time on Wednesday.</p>
